      "low users to trade contracts based on temperature movements or precipitation amounts in specific cities, from New York City to Los Angeles. Traders can take positions on whether a city will reach a certain high temperature or fall within a particular range. Each weather market names its official settlement source in its market rules. Daily high/low temperature markets settle based on the final climate report issued by the National Weather Service (NWS), typically released the following morning. Hourly temperature markets settle on readings from <a href=\"https://weather.com/kalshi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">The Weather Company</a>. Always check the specific market\u2019s rules for its source.</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p> </p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-heading intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h1 id=\"h_13a85c056f\">How Do I Trade on Weather Markets?</h1></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Kalshi creates a prediction market around a specific temperature threshold for a given location. For example: \u201cHighest temperature in Chicago on April 15, 2025?\u201d<br/>\u200b<br/>Contract prices for temperature ranges may shift as new weather data (e.g., forecasts, model runs, satellite images, observations) becomes available.</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-callout\" style=\"background-color:#feedaf80;border-color:#fbc91633\"><div clas",
      "interblocks-callout\" style=\"background-color:#feedaf80;border-color:#fbc91633\"><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p><b>Note:</b> Not all weather data is the same. Apps like AccuWeather, iOS Weather, or Google Weather may be useful for guidance but do not determine contract outcomes. The only source used for settlement is the one named in the market\u2019s rules - the NWS Daily Climate Report for daily temperature markets, or The Weather Company for hourly temperature markets.</p></div></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_e6219cfd03\">Daily Temperature Markets</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Daily weather markets are typically ranges: contracts resolve on the day\u2019s highest (or lowest) temperature at the listed station, offered as a set of temperature ranges plus \u201cor above\u201d / \u201cor below\u201d levels.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>These markets settle the next morning based on the high temperature recorded in the final NWS Daily Climate Report. Market determination may be delayed in the rare instances of a) a high temperature is not consistent with 6-hr or 24-hr highs reported by METAR or b) the final NWS Climate Report high temperature value is lower than previous preliminary report.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 i",
      "erblocks-align-left\"><p>These markets settle the next morning based on the high temperature recorded in the final NWS Daily Climate Report. Market determination may be delayed in the rare instances of a) a high temperature is not consistent with 6-hr or 24-hr highs reported by METAR or b) the final NWS Climate Report high temperature value is lower than previous preliminary report.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_e3c3987fb7\">Hourly Temperature Markets</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Some temperature markets are hourly - the market title names an exact time, for example \u201cChicago temperature at 5 PM EDT.\u201d These markets are also directional: each contract resolves on whether the temperature at that time is above or below a specific level, rather than within a range. They settle on the temperature at that exact time as reported by The Weather Company for the station coordinates named in the market rules (for example, KORD for Chicago).<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>For these markets, The Weather Company\u2019s reported value is official and final. NWS Climatological Reports, Google Weather, and other services may be useful references, but they are not authoritative for settlement. Preliminary Weather Company readings may differ from the final reported value due to rounding and",
      "ation may be delayed in the rare instances of a) a high temperature is not consistent with 6-hr or 24-hr highs reported by METAR or b) the final NWS Climate Report high temperature value is lower than previous preliminary report.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_e3c3987fb7\">Hourly Temperature Markets</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Some temperature markets are hourly - the market title names an exact time, for example \u201cChicago temperature at 5 PM EDT.\u201d These markets are also directional: each contract resolves on whether the temperature at that time is above or below a specific level, rather than within a range. They settle on the temperature at that exact time as reported by The Weather Company for the station coordinates named in the market rules (for example, KORD for Chicago).<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>For these markets, The Weather Company\u2019s reported value is official and final. NWS Climatological Reports, Google Weather, and other services may be useful references, but they are not authoritative for settlement. Preliminary Weather Company readings may differ from the final reported value due to rounding and conversion, so use caution when interpreting preliminary readings.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblock",
      "1789857900&amp;signature=1b4fd6d2115a10f60a4a997a4bba27bebb7ccc217bd6dd1ec3c8900a2caf682f&amp;req=diAuF8p2nIJWWvMW1HO4zcK36ymsyrsE%2B8It%2FPAV8Auv5QPZqfA4vt6Q8iaN%0A8fjwCSJZfGnGX4LDu%2F0%3D%0A\" alt=\"\"/></a></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p><i>*Make sure you are viewing the temperature from the same date as the Kalshi market.</i><br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>For hourly temperature markets, the outcome source data is available at <a href=\"https://weather.com/kalshi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">weather.com/kalshi</a>.</p></div><section class=\"jsx-62724fba150252e0 related_articles my-6\"><hr class=\"jsx-62724fba150252e0 my-6 sm:my-8\"/><div class=\"jsx-62724fba150252e0 mb-3 text-xl font-bold\">Related Articles</div><section class=\"flex flex-col rounded-card border border-solid border-card-border bg-card-bg p-2 sm:p-3 -mx-5 sm:-mx-6\"><ul role=\"list\" class=\"!m-0 list-none !p-0\"><li class=\"!m-0 !list-none\"><a class=\"duration-250 group/article flex flex-row justify-between gap-2 py-2 no-underline transition ease-linear hover:bg-primary-alpha-10 hover:text-primary sm:rounded-card-inner sm:py-3 -mx-2 rounded-none px-5 py-3 sm:m-0 sm:px-3\" href=\"https://help.kalshi.com/en/articles/13823763-what-is-kalshi\" data-testid=\"article-link\"><div class=\"flex flex-col p-0\"><span class=\"m-0 text-md text-body-primary-color group-hover/article:text-"
