      "-align-left\"><p>For these markets, The Weather Company\u2019s reported value is official and final. NWS Climatological Reports, Google Weather, and other services may be useful references, but they are not authoritative for settlement. Preliminary Weather Company readings may differ from the final reported value due to rounding and conversion, so use caution when interpreting preliminary readings.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Settlement processes approximately 25-35 minutes after the market closes to ensure accurate data retrieval from the official source - a short delay after close is normal. Historical readings and market data are available at <a href=\"https://weather.com/kalshi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">weather.com/kalshi</a>.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_43c2973c54\">Daylight Savings Time</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>The NWS Climate Reports (used for daily temperature markets) use local standard time when reporting daily high temperatures. This means that during Daylight Saving Time, the high temperature will be recorded between 1:00 AM and 12:59 AM local time the following day - not based on the standard midnight-to-midnight range.</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p> </p></d",
      "\",\"author\":null,\"blocks\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"How do weather markets work?\",\"idAttribute\":\"h_3a878115eb\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Kalshi offers a wide variety of weather-related markets that allow users to trade contracts based on temperature movements or precipitation amounts in specific cities, from New York City to Los Angeles. Traders can take positions on whether a city will reach a certain high temperature or fall within a particular range. Each weather market names its official settlement source in its market rules. Daily high/low temperature markets settle based on the final climate report issued by the National Weather Service (NWS), typically released the following morning. Hourly temperature markets settle on readings from \\u003ca href=\\\"https://weather.com/kalshi\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003eThe Weather Company\\u003c/a\\u003e. Always check the specific market\u2019s rules for its source.\",\"class\":\"no-margin\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\" \",\"class\":\"no-margin\"},{\"type\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"How Do I Trade on Weather Markets?\",\"idAttribute\":\"h_13a85c056f\"},{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"text\":\"Kalshi creates a prediction market around a specific temperature threshold for a given location. For example: \u201cHighest temperature in Chicago on April 15, 2025?\u201d\\u003cbr\\u003e\u200b\\u003cbr\\u003eContract prices for temperature ranges may shift as new weather data (e.g., forecasts, model runs, satellite images, observations) becomes available.\",\"class\":\"no-mar"
