      "pitation amounts in specific cities, from New York City to Los Angeles. Traders can take positions on whether a city will reach a certain high temperature or fall within a particular range. Each weather market names its official settlement source in its market rules. Daily high/low temperature markets settle based on the final climate report issued by the National Weather Service (NWS), typically released the following morning. Hourly temperature markets settle on readings from <a href=\"https://weather.com/kalshi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">The Weather Company</a>. Always check the specific market\u2019s rules for its source.</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p> </p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-heading intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h1 id=\"h_13a85c056f\">How Do I Trade on Weather Markets?</h1></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Kalshi creates a prediction market around a specific temperature threshold for a given location. For example: \u201cHighest temperature in Chicago on April 15, 2025?\u201d<br/>\u200b<br/>Contract prices for temperature ranges may shift as new weather data (e.g., forecasts, model runs, satellite images, observations) becomes available.</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-callout\" style=\"background-color:#feedaf80;border-color:#fbc91633\"><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-ali",
      "y Weather Company readings may differ from the final reported value due to rounding and conversion, so use caution when interpreting preliminary readings.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Settlement processes approximately 25-35 minutes after the market closes to ensure accurate data retrieval from the official source - a short delay after close is normal. Historical readings and market data are available at <a href=\"https://weather.com/kalshi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">weather.com/kalshi</a>.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_43c2973c54\">Daylight Savings Time</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>The NWS Climate Reports (used for daily temperature markets) use local standard time when reporting daily high temperatures. This means that during Daylight Saving Time, the high temperature will be recorded between 1:00 AM and 12:59 AM local time the following day - not based on the standard midnight-to-midnight range.</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p> </p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_b566fad15f\">Finding Kalshi market&#x27;s relevant source information</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-image intercom-interblocks-align-left\"",
      "to rounding and conversion, so use caution when interpreting preliminary readings.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>Settlement processes approximately 25-35 minutes after the market closes to ensure accurate data retrieval from the official source - a short delay after close is normal. Historical readings and market data are available at <a href=\"https://weather.com/kalshi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">weather.com/kalshi</a>.<br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_43c2973c54\">Daylight Savings Time</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>The NWS Climate Reports (used for daily temperature markets) use local standard time when reporting daily high temperatures. This means that during Daylight Saving Time, the high temperature will be recorded between 1:00 AM and 12:59 AM local time the following day - not based on the standard midnight-to-midnight range.</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p> </p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-subheading3 intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><h3 id=\"h_b566fad15f\">Finding Kalshi market&#x27;s relevant source information</h3></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-image intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><a href=\"https://kalshi-62603e0948a4.intercom-attachments-7.com/i/o/ww",
      "682f&amp;req=diAuF8p2nIJWWvMW1HO4zcK36ymsyrsE%2B8It%2FPAV8Auv5QPZqfA4vt6Q8iaN%0A8fjwCSJZfGnGX4LDu%2F0%3D%0A\" alt=\"\"/></a></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p><i>*Make sure you are viewing the temperature from the same date as the Kalshi market.</i><br/>\u200b</p></div><div class=\"intercom-interblocks-paragraph no-margin intercom-interblocks-align-left\"><p>For hourly temperature markets, the outcome source data is available at <a href=\"https://weather.com/kalshi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">weather.com/kalshi</a>.</p></div><section class=\"jsx-62724fba150252e0 related_articles my-6\"><hr class=\"jsx-62724fba150252e0 my-6 sm:my-8\"/><div class=\"jsx-62724fba150252e0 mb-3 text-xl font-bold\">Related Articles</div><section class=\"flex flex-col rounded-card border border-solid border-card-border bg-card-bg p-2 sm:p-3 -mx-5 sm:-mx-6\"><ul role=\"list\" class=\"!m-0 list-none !p-0\"><li class=\"!m-0 !list-none\"><a class=\"duration-250 group/article flex flex-row justify-between gap-2 py-2 no-underline transition ease-linear hover:bg-primary-alpha-10 hover:text-primary sm:rounded-card-inner sm:py-3 -mx-2 rounded-none px-5 py-3 sm:m-0 sm:px-3\" href=\"https://help.kalshi.com/en/articles/13823763-what-is-kalshi\" data-testid=\"article-link\"><div class=\"flex flex-col p-0\"><span class=\"m-0 text-md text-body-primary-color group-hover/article:text-primary\">What is Kalshi?</span></div><div class=\"flex shrink-0 flex-col justify-cente",
